{
  "chapter.63A7B1E69BE2C38A.title": "I · A Light Among Ruins",
  "quest.3C1A37141ABD78D8.title": "A page without a place",
  "quest.3C1A37141ABD78D8.quest_desc": [
    "A place to return",
    "",
    "An unsigned page whispers: 'A place begins when someone decides to return.' Choose a site with water, wood and room to grow.",
    "Open quests with F8 or the book icon in your inventory. If you change the binding, find Quests in Controls. Read, then confirm; this optional acknowledgement does not advance the campaign."
  ],
  "quest.3AC9E31D78B2BCB0.title": "Somewhere to begin",
  "quest.3AC9E31D78B2BCB0.quest_desc": [
    "A place to return",
    "",
    "Build a crafting table. Before making a new tool, inspect its recipe and uses in the recipe viewer. The Atlas can remember a hundred destinations; a workbench gives you the means to reach the first."
  ],
  "quest.153F660992CE9BA3.title": "Read the stone",
  "quest.153F660992CE9BA3.quest_desc": [
    "A place to return",
    "",
    "Make a stone pickaxe and inspect the block information overlay before mining unfamiliar ore. Tool requirements matter. Keep your wooden tool only if you still need it; the expedition is easier with a clear inventory."
  ],
  "quest.0CA82678D5DFA3E8.title": "A recipe worth keeping",
  "quest.0CA82678D5DFA3E8.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Open the recipe viewer and bookmark a recipe you plan to make next. Look up the viewer's bindings in Controls instead of guessing a key. Bookmarks are your shopping list; remove finished projects so the list stays useful. Confirm after trying it."
  ],
  "quest.2742A6E0D4B75C80.title": "A shelf for tomorrow",
  "quest.2742A6E0D4B75C80.quest_desc": [
    "A place to return",
    "",
    "Make a chest. Separate supplies for your next project from things you are collecting for later. Try the installed sorting and matching-deposit controls on ordinary materials first. Comfortable storage is available now; its purpose is to save attention."
  ],
  "quest.216E7E97E831A00C.title": "Heat with a purpose",
  "quest.216E7E97E831A00C.quest_desc": [
    "A place to return",
    "",
    "Build a furnace and cook or smelt a useful batch. Fuel keeps burning once lit, so prepare the inputs before starting. Later workshops will automate this same pattern: supply, transformation, collection."
  ],
  "quest.73220D1B896D7CD9.title": "The edge of the dark",
  "quest.73220D1B896D7CD9.quest_desc": [
    "A place to return",
    "",
    "Prepare eight torches. Light the path between your entrance, water and work area before expanding underground. A lit route is also a promise: you intend to come back along it."
  ],
  "quest.4FC6DEBD8FEED1C0.title": "A return address",
  "quest.4FC6DEBD8FEED1C0.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Place and use a bed when you can obtain wool safely. Check that the respawn space is clear. In co-op, tell your companions where the shelter is. This optional practice does not require hunting sheep immediately."
  ],
  "quest.34262755FE4ACAB3.title": "The Atlas listens",
  "quest.34262755FE4ACAB3.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "The cover warms. 'Make room for those who have not arrived.'",
    "Click this milestone's task to open the Atlas. Select The Atlas Awakens, read its materials and choose Deliver. The first delivery gives your team a portable Atlas. Use the item to return to this screen; its crafting recipe is for replacements and gifts."
  ],
  "quest.744122ED817C45E5.title": "Carry the river",
  "quest.744122ED817C45E5.quest_desc": [
    "Welcome the travellers",
    "",
    "Smelt enough iron for a bucket. Carry water to a small farm near the shelter; hydrated farmland supports reliable food production. Keep the water accessible for future recipes and emergencies."
  ],
  "quest.4E81EB4CAA1D1D13.title": "The patient part",
  "quest.4E81EB4CAA1D1D13.quest_desc": [
    "Welcome the travellers",
    "",
    "Harvest three wheat and replant before leaving. A tiny maintained plot beats a huge forgotten field. Save seeds separately from food so one hurried inventory transfer does not empty the next harvest."
  ],
  "quest.0DDC984DEA3CAD80.title": "A kitchen tool",
  "quest.0DDC984DEA3CAD80.quest_desc": [
    "Welcome the travellers",
    "",
    "Make a flint knife. Inspect its uses: Farmer's Delight knives take part in cutting-board recipes and gathering certain ingredients. Choose the recipe you need before spending durability on random plants."
  ],
  "quest.1EE8E17F9022A402.title": "A different kind of crafting",
  "quest.1EE8E17F9022A402.quest_desc": [
    "Welcome the travellers",
    "",
    "Place a cutting board and inspect a recipe that uses it. Put down the ingredient, then use the indicated tool. The board is a workstation with its own interactions; an ordinary crafting grid cannot replace it."
  ],
  "quest.7CD0636D9B7DDA5E.title": "Four places at the table",
  "quest.7CD0636D9B7DDA5E.quest_desc": [
    "Welcome the travellers",
    "",
    "Prepare four bowls. Some meals return their container after eating; account for containers when planning a batch. Mara's margin note reads: 'A kitchen is measured by the people it can welcome.'"
  ],
  "quest.7022698D6AF61048.title": "Food before distance",
  "quest.7022698D6AF61048.quest_desc": [
    "Welcome the travellers",
    "",
    "Prepare three bread for the short survey. Watch both hunger and saturation information: a fuller hunger bar alone does not describe how long a meal will sustain you. Keep a reserve at home."
  ],
  "quest.5E980BB86AE535DF.title": "A table for those returning",
  "quest.5E980BB86AE535DF.quest_desc": [
    "Welcome the travellers",
    "",
    "Mara left a place at the table for a stranger. Keep this kitchen: future expeditions will need it.",
    "Open the Atlas, select A Table for Travellers and check the available and missing materials before choosing Deliver. This first version checks the delivery, not your kitchen's layout."
  ],
  "quest.0E2E2C08C06F343B.title": "Metal that remembers weather",
  "quest.0E2E2C08C06F343B.quest_desc": [
    "Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Smelt four copper ingots. The old instruments used copper frames: easy to shape, easy to recognise. Store the ingots with the glass for the lens project instead of scattering them across chests."
  ],
  "quest.27B833739C94F3B1.title": "A window small enough to carry",
  "quest.27B833739C94F3B1.quest_desc": [
    "Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Smelt four glass. Take sand from a small, safe patch rather than undermining the bank beside your shelter. The lens starts with common materials; careful assembly will give them their purpose."
  ],
  "quest.7D9F3FDD50B52514.title": "A borrowed horizon",
  "quest.7D9F3FDD50B52514.quest_desc": [
    "Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Ivo wrote beside the sketch: 'Measure before believing.'",
    "Open the Atlas and select Assemble the Lens. Deliver the listed materials to receive the lens once. You do not need to craft another one for this project. Keep it for the first signal; the recipe remains available for replacements."
  ],
  "quest.67D63EA89ED72879.title": "Mark the ordinary",
  "quest.67D63EA89ED72879.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Find the installed map controls and mark your shelter. Give the marker a practical name. Check the route home before leaving; a map is useful because it records your world, even when the Atlas remembers another one."
  ],
  "quest.078C1FA519669777.title": "Leave with a question",
  "quest.078C1FA519669777.quest_desc": [
    "Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Prepare three paper for field notes. Carry food, a pickaxe and light, leaving space for samples. Choose a nearby stretch of ground you can return from before supplies run low. This is a survey, not a race to a distant dimension."
  ],
  "quest.42845362110B95B7.title": "Two accounts of one place",
  "quest.42845362110B95B7.quest_desc": [
    "Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Take a short walk. Compare one nearby landmark with your map, then return while you still have supplies.",
    "In the Atlas, select Field Survey and Deliver its supplies to receive your notes. This version checks materials; the walk is suggested practice without a distance requirement. Keep the notes for the signal."
  ],
  "quest.5625EFC0A0C376CF.title": "The expedition ends at home",
  "quest.5625EFC0A0C376CF.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "After your outing, replenish food and torches before storing the rest. Try matching-deposit without moving the supplies you want to carry. Write down one missing material for the next trip. A good return makes the next departure easier."
  ],
  "quest.762B0B9FB46F552F.title": "One light answers",
  "quest.762B0B9FB46F552F.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "The Atlas records a distant light answering. Someone listened, or something remembers how.",
    "Open First Signal in the Atlas and Deliver the listed materials. Your team receives a signal core once. Use it to build a survey station: the light now has a place in your home, and your compass can remember the way back."
  ],
  "quest.258FF615C9AD9711.title": "A workshop with a destination",
  "quest.258FF615C9AD9711.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "Your workshop has a destination. Keep the kitchen, shelves and survey kit useful as you explore the lost crafts.",
    "Once every project in this act is delivered, choose Advance in the Atlas to open the next act. If a response takes too long, choose Refresh before trying again. This closing reading grants no reward."
  ],
  "quest.2E22D95F3AC6BE45.title": "A place your compass remembers",
  "quest.2E22D95F3AC6BE45.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "Build a survey station with the signal core, copper, smooth stone and glass; the recipe viewer shows their arrangement. Place it somewhere worth returning to.",
    "Use a compass on the station to mark these coordinates without consuming the compass. It points here while you are in the same dimension. Moving or removing the station does not move the mark: use the compass on a station again to update it. An empty hand opens your current team’s Atlas.",
    "Share marked compasses with your companions. A gifted station works too; using it does not complete campaign projects."
  ],
  "chapter.0F7AE2DC86CB6F50.title": "II · The Lost Crafts",
  "quest.048D2E6A70144A24.title": "Four benches, one workshop",
  "quest.048D2E6A70144A24.quest_desc": [
    "The shared workshop",
    "",
    "The signal carries four overlapping notes. Ivo describes a measuring bench; Mara lists meals; another page sketches crystals beside a growing bed. The Atlas cannot yet place them in the same room.",
    "Choose any branch. Open a hexagonal task to consult the Atlas: only an explicit project delivery changes your team's campaign. Inventory checks and optional acknowledgements teach the route; gifts remain useful. This reading is self-reported."
  ],
  "quest.1C29DD1E3979A642.title": "Let water do the turning",
  "quest.1C29DD1E3979A642.quest_desc": [
    "Ivo · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Ivo's note starts with a stream, not a furnace. Craft a Create water wheel from planks around a shaft, then use its Ponder scene to arrange flowing water and connect a shaft.",
    "A turning wheel supplies rotation, not electrical energy. Leave room for the press and a safe walking path. This task detects the wheel in inventory; it does not inspect water or a working installation."
  ],
  "quest.505AD15489797C5A.title": "An iron ingot, made flat",
  "quest.505AD15489797C5A.quest_desc": [
    "Ivo · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Connect a mechanical press to rotation and place a depot beneath its head as shown in Ponder. The press itself uses a shaft, an andesite casing and an iron block.",
    "Pressing iron ingots produces Create iron sheets. Make two for a calibration frame. Keep the press installed: the Atlas asks for a prototype, not your machinery. Possession of the press only completes this tutorial task."
  ],
  "quest.24DF7B8F88C1FCB9.title": "Read the strain",
  "quest.24DF7B8F88C1FCB9.quest_desc": [
    "Ivo · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Ivo crossed out 'turn it faster' and wrote 'measure first'. Engineer's Goggles use glass, string and a gold plate. Consult the loaded recipe and use the press you already built for its metalwork.",
    "Wear them and inspect a connected machine: compare speed and stress information before adding another consumer. More speed can increase demand. This inventory task does not claim that a measurement was made."
  ],
  "quest.5C34E7D93BAD4D93.title": "Wire without a factory",
  "quest.5C34E7D93BAD4D93.quest_desc": [
    "Ivo · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "The copper sketch offers a hand route. Immersive Engineering's hammer turns a copper ingot into a plate; its wirecutters turn a copper plate into copper wire. Consult both crafting recipes.",
    "Make two wires for the frame. A metal press is a later alternative, not a requirement here. Wire is a material; it is not the same item as a wire coil used to connect electrical equipment."
  ],
  "quest.5F676C980602FEFF.title": "A Measure of Iron",
  "quest.5F676C980602FEFF.quest_desc": [
    "Ivo · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Ivo's prototype joins two iron sheets, two copper wires and a raw lens into one calibration frame. This is a shared standard: hand tools and rotating machines contribute different parts.",
    "Open this task's Atlas page and deliver one frame for precision_bench. The frame is consumed; machines stay in the world. A second frame is needed for the living matrix. Receiving a frame is allowed, but only delivery records the milestone."
  ],
  "quest.1AF624DC63ABDC33.title": "A small electrical beginning",
  "quest.1AF624DC63ABDC33.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "A soot-stained page describes a coal generator beside a workbench. Actually Additions uses iron casings here; their recipe includes black quartz, iron and wooden rods. Check that supply before building.",
    "The generator is an early fuel-based energy source. Plan a short connection to the reconstructor using the mod's instructions, and keep spare fuel nearby. This task detects a generator, not sustained power output."
  ],
  "quest.4E94D46197FC6BC3.title": "A beam with a job",
  "quest.4E94D46197FC6BC3.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "The Atomic Reconstructor uses an iron casing, iron and redstone. Build it and read its entry before placing material in the beam's path; arrange a controlled test area where dropped items can be recovered.",
    "Supply energy and experiment with one redstone dust first. Keep the machine: the project's delivery is an energy coupler. This possession check does not certify beam operation or electrical wiring."
  ],
  "quest.5525FEC32B117FD6.title": "Redstone remembers another shape",
  "quest.5525FEC32B117FD6.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "The pinned laser recipe converts redstone dust into a Restonia crystal for 40 energy units. Start with a small batch and recover the result before processing more. This is ordinary Restonia, not empowered Restonia.",
    "Reserve two crystals, one iron casing and two Create andesite alloys for an energy coupler. The recipe gives early electricity a lasting material role without asking for a large power plant."
  ],
  "quest.5281CA2BAADED9DF.title": "A Crystal Connection",
  "quest.5281CA2BAADED9DF.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "The Atlas aligns Ivo's marks with the crystal notes: neither page supplies the whole instrument. Craft one energy coupler from the Restonia, casing and andesite-alloy route.",
    "Open the Atlas here and deliver one coupler for crystal_grid. It is consumed once; your generator and reconstructor remain installed. Tutorials can be completed with gifted items, but campaign completion always comes from this authoritative delivery."
  ],
  "quest.13D42DB7A4E29182.title": "Write a first working spell",
  "quest.13D42DB7A4E29182.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "A novice spell book is made with a book and an iron shovel, pickaxe, axe and sword. Use ordinary spare tools and inspect the recipe before committing equipment you still need.",
    "Read the spell-building instructions and try an available utility spell in a safe place. Ivo's margin asks the same question as at the press: what changed, and can you repeat it? The task checks only possession of the book."
  ],
  "quest.1751AC5350F46D6C.title": "Keep a source-gem reserve",
  "quest.1751AC5350F46D6C.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "Ars source gems become tools, apparatus parts and crop inputs. The imbuement recipes accept amethyst or lapis; the chamber uses archwood planks and gold. Follow its guide for operation and reserve gems before expanding your workshop.",
    "The living matrix needs two source gems; making magebloom seeds also uses gems. A source gem is a material, not a charged Source storage device. This inventory check does not measure magical energy."
  ],
  "quest.0D777B65AE7AD4C0.title": "A crop with workshop uses",
  "quest.0D777B65AE7AD4C0.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "The Enchanting Apparatus recipe uses a seed as reagent with four source gems on pedestals to produce magebloom seeds; its listed Source cost is zero. The apparatus itself needs a diamond, gold and sourcestone: plan that expedition first. Follow its guide for the required arrangement; a zero recipe cost does not make the apparatus free.",
    "Grow and harvest magebloom, then craft one bloom into four fibers. Reserve two fibers for a living matrix. Keep the planting area: this crop should supply future work, not vanish into a one-off errand."
  ],
  "quest.7A2C3D602817EC20.title": "The living workshop",
  "quest.7A2C3D602817EC20.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "The new page overlays a planting bed with Ivo's measuring marks. Craft a living matrix from two magebloom fibers, two source gems and a calibration frame. Make a fresh frame: the bench project already consumed its own.",
    "Deliver one matrix through the Atlas for living_workshop after precision_bench. The matrix is consumed; your crop and apparatus remain. The server checks the prerequisites, even if someone gives you a finished matrix early."
  ],
  "quest.60274F8FAAB2F834.title": "Mara keeps the kitchen working",
  "quest.60274F8FAAB2F834.quest_desc": [
    "Mara · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Mara's inventory lists a cooking pot before a second machine. Farmer's Delight uses iron, bricks, a water bucket and a wooden shovel. Read the pot's recipe and place it above a suitable heat source.",
    "Choose a meal you can supply from nearby crops and practice making a batch. The pantry prototype has its own recipe; the pot is useful kitchen infrastructure, not an item the project consumes."
  ],
  "quest.53F96B4513813835.title": "Use the catch",
  "quest.53F96B4513813835.quest_desc": [
    "Mara · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Aquaculture has its own filleting knives and fish fillets. Follow the loaded recipes for a catch you can obtain; do not assume every fish or every knife uses the same processing route.",
    "Raw fish fillets can be cooked over a campfire; the pinned recipe takes 600 ticks. A furnace or smoker offers other listed routes. Reserve cooked fillets for travel provisions while keeping a meal for yourself."
  ],
  "quest.7B649EF9ED27AC7F.title": "Pack a real travelling meal",
  "quest.7B649EF9ED27AC7F.quest_desc": [
    "Mara · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Mara's bundle combines pantry staples with the fishing branch. Two vegetable soups and two cooked Aquaculture fish fillets make one bundle. Inspect the soup recipe for carrot, potato, beetroot and leafy-green tags; keep extra food for your next outing.",
    "The bundle is a crafted project material, not a promise of automatic hunger refill or an endless lunchbox. Detecting it here does not submit it. Keep the kitchen and fishing tools available for the next batch."
  ],
  "quest.774DD93299251487.title": "The travelling pantry",
  "quest.774DD93299251487.quest_desc": [
    "Mara · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Mara's note ends with a practical correction: 'Count the people who return, not only the crates that leave.' The kitchen and fishing route now contribute to the same workshop as copper and crystals.",
    "Open the Atlas and deliver one ration bundle for travelling_pantry. The bundle is consumed. No cooking pot, fishing rod or other installed equipment is collected. Keep extra personal food outside the delivery."
  ],
  "quest.3E9B76FA05037B25.title": "Can the next person repeat it?",
  "quest.3E9B76FA05037B25.quest_desc": [
    "Ivo · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Optional demonstration: process a second iron ingot at the press, retrieve its sheet and label the input/output area. Leave a note describing the wheel connection and what to check if rotation stops.",
    "Confirm only after trying it. This is a self-reported installation exercise: no scanner checks your build, it grants no reward and it never completes a campaign milestone. A gift does not replace the experiment."
  ],
  "quest.453C69E2CF5980E2.title": "Leave the bed ready",
  "quest.453C69E2CF5980E2.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "Optional demonstration: harvest a small magebloom batch, process some fibers and leave a planted bed ready for the next visit. Store seeds and spare fibers separately so a prototype does not consume your whole reserve.",
    "This checkbox records your own report, not growth, chunk activity or automatic production. There is no offline upkeep requirement. Mara's test is simple: could someone else make the next batch without rebuilding everything?"
  ],
  "quest.069839E9FD2685EE.title": "The room in the records",
  "quest.069839E9FD2685EE.quest_desc": [
    "The shared workshop",
    "",
    "With all four projects delivered, the pages finally agree on a room: a workshop where no single craft could replace the others. The signal was carrying the work of several people, not a blueprint for one perfect machine.",
    "Bring three paper and one copper ingot to the Atlas and deliver lost_workshop. These archive supplies are consumed; the four completed projects remain recorded. This closes the act-II archive, not the full pack campaign."
  ],
  "quest.3D2B82152F596665.title": "A workshop worth connecting",
  "quest.3D2B82152F596665.quest_desc": [
    "The shared workshop",
    "",
    "The Atlas marks four benches with one shared doorway. Before expanding, choose a supply route worth improving: sheets, crystals, fibers or provisions. Keep the other benches useful instead of tearing them down for the next tier.",
    "This optional reflection is self-reported. Check the Atlas for available advancement; later acts remain under development in this slice. Completing this checkbox does not unlock them, create resources or advance the server campaign."
  ],
  "chapter.778667D17CE889F6.title": "III · Routes of Exchange",
  "quest.37439F67D72711CE.title": "The silence between workshops",
  "quest.37439F67D72711CE.quest_desc": [
    "Sera · Local connections",
    "",
    "Sera marked five short routes before drawing a central tower. The first failures were local: a missing delivery, a full shelf, a workshop waiting for a part. Rebuild connections that can be repaired from either end.",
    "Hexagons open the Atlas. Only explicit delivery consumes a prototype and advances the team; gifts are valid. Inventory tutorials consume nothing and do not prove working installations. Round exercises are optional personal observations. You can deliver without completing them."
  ],
  "quest.6B801E1DFD8835ED.title": "Presses from the fallen sky",
  "quest.6B801E1DFD8835ED.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Break the mysterious cube at a meteorite center without Silk Touch to obtain the four AE2 presses. A meteorite compass, made by charging a normal compass, points toward a cube; consult the AE2 guide. Use the powered Inscriber to print logic and silicon parts, then combine them with redstone.",
    "Reserve two finished logic processors. If assembly stalls, compare the three slots and power supply: a printed logic circuit is only an intermediate."
  ],
  "quest.67715DD11D530227.title": "A board takes several benches",
  "quest.67715DD11D530227.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "PneumaticCraft assembles a PCB from an unassembled board, two capacitors and two transistors. Follow the plastic, UV exposure and etching-acid route in its guide. The empty PCB needs 1.5 bar; capacitors, transistors and etching acid need 1.0 bar. Consult each pressure-chamber recipe and the guide for safe operation. The Amadron PCB blueprint costs eight emeralds; plan that purchase before automation.",
    "An assembly laser is not the starting route. If crafting fails, check whether your board is still blank or unassembled, and consult the pressure-control guide before changing machinery."
  ],
  "quest.34E8C304216AA748.title": "A blue signal",
  "quest.34E8C304216AA748.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Return to the Atomic Reconstructor. Its laser converts lapis into ordinary Palis crystal for 40 energy units; empowered Palis is a different material. Process a small recoverable batch.",
    "Two Palis crystals join two logic processors, one PCB and one calibration frame in a routing matrix. Plan a second matrix for the inventory sensor after delivering the first."
  ],
  "quest.3E5FB620D650D35E.title": "Budget the first crystal",
  "quest.3E5FB620D650D35E.quest_desc": [
    "Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Four Inferium around an infusion crystal produce one Prudentium. The ordinary crystal itself costs a diamond, four prosperity shards and four Inferium. Budget eight additional Inferium for two Prudentium.",
    "Keep planting supplies instead of converting everything at once. Mining can supply a beginning; crops can replenish it. If crafting stops, check the crystal recipe and remaining durability."
  ],
  "quest.6FF1C6BDC6CF1D6A.title": "Wax from an ordinary hive",
  "quest.6FF1C6BDC6CF1D6A.quest_desc": [
    "Supplies that return",
    "",
    "The basic Productive Bees centrifuge processes ordinary Minecraft honeycomb into wax. Its construction uses iron and a grindstone; follow the loaded recipe and operating guide. Specialized breeding is not required for these two wax.",
    "Leave access to the hive and flowers for another harvest. If a comb is rejected, inspect its exact recipe rather than assuming all resource and decorative combs process alike."
  ],
  "quest.7E5DA638A8AF99BA.title": "The old garden contributes",
  "quest.7E5DA638A8AF99BA.quest_desc": [
    "Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Make another living matrix: one calibration frame, two source gems and two magebloom fibers. The matrix delivered in Act II was consumed; completed history does not supply its replacement.",
    "Combine this matrix with two Prudentium and two wax for a propagation core. Keep the growing beds and hive. This material recipe does not automatically plant crops or unlock every resource species."
  ],
  "quest.1AAAAA6B2E1E4563.title": "Osmium learns a signal",
  "quest.1AAAAA6B2E1E4563.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful power",
    "",
    "Mekanism infuses an osmium ingot with 20 units of redstone infusion to make a basic control circuit. Supply the Metallurgic Infuser with energy and the correct infusion material. Make two circuits for a regulator.",
    "If processing stalls, inspect the stored infusion type and energy before adding unrelated dusts. A small fuel generator can begin a modest batch; a reactor is unnecessary."
  ],
  "quest.597D8746CE914B5A.title": "Steel without a giant furnace",
  "quest.597D8746CE914B5A.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful power",
    "",
    "A steel ingot and the Immersive Engineering hammer make one steel plate. Mekanism offers an early route: carbon-infuse iron into enriched iron, infuse again into steel dust, then smelt it. Check each recipe before filling the infuser.",
    "Reserve two plates. An IE steelworks is an alternative investment; a blast furnace is not required just for this batch. Enriched iron is not yet a finished steel ingot."
  ],
  "quest.5D719D69593E262A.title": "A coupling, not a power plant",
  "quest.5D719D69593E262A.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful power",
    "",
    "Rebuild the energy coupler from two Restonia crystals, one iron casing and two andesite alloys. It remains the bridge from the first powered workshop.",
    "Two basic circuits and two steel plates join the coupler in a regulator. Plan another regulator for the handling core: delivering this first prototype consumes it, while generators and machines stay installed."
  ],
  "quest.16E8D490AF70ABCE.title": "Read the tree before the shelf",
  "quest.16E8D490AF70ABCE.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "The Integrated Dynamics Squeezer extracts 1000 mB of Menril resin from a Menril log. A Drying Basin turns that amount into a crystallized Menril block; crafting that block yields nine chunks. Follow the guide for manual squeezing and fluid transfer.",
    "Reserve two chunks. Mechanical machines are later alternatives. If the basin stays idle, check resin type and amount; ordinary logs cannot replace Menril."
  ],
  "quest.4D75C5943C18E96B.title": "Bake the logic",
  "quest.4D75C5943C18E96B.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "LaserIO makes four raw logic chips from a quartz block, clay balls, gold nuggets and redstone. Smelt the raw chips into finished chips; the sensor needs two. Plan quartz acquisition before promising this delivery.",
    "A raw chip will not satisfy the integration recipe. Keep the other chips for network equipment and compare the item name with the recipe if your crafting grid shows no output."
  ],
  "quest.601DDFCEB1D5FEA2.title": "A second matrix has a job",
  "quest.601DDFCEB1D5FEA2.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "The routing matrix delivered for A Shared Language has been consumed. Make or receive another from two logic processors, one PCB, two Palis crystals and one calibration frame.",
    "Combine it with two crystallized Menril chunks and two finished LaserIO chips for an inventory sensor. Both systems contribute materials, while your transport installation can use the network you prefer."
  ],
  "quest.7C4CA98F4865E101.title": "Paper tells the hands",
  "quest.7C4CA98F4865E101.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Modular Routers makes six blank modules from paper, gold nuggets and redstone. Reserve two blanks for the handling core; blanks are ingredients, not configured transfer instructions.",
    "Use the rest for specific jobs described in the router guide. If a router does nothing, inspect the installed module function and target rather than expecting a blank module to move items."
  ],
  "quest.130D7A6D79505C81.title": "Five careful passes",
  "quest.130D7A6D79505C81.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Start a Create precision mechanism with a gold plate. Deploy a small cogwheel, a large cogwheel and an iron nugget in order, repeating five times. Consult Ponder: deployers need brass hands, and brass uses heated mixing.",
    "The final result is probabilistic. Prepare spare inputs and retain incomplete mechanisms for the next pass. One reusable station can repeat the sequence; a long automatic belt is optional. Check the final item before counting success."
  ],
  "quest.4634B9599F78810B.title": "A regulator for the hands",
  "quest.4634B9599F78810B.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Make a second power regulator from two basic circuits, two steel plates and an energy coupler. The first delivery stays completed, but its token cannot also become an ingredient.",
    "Combine this regulator with two blank modules and one finished precision mechanism for the handling core. Gifts are valid: these routes exchange useful work, not proof of who held every tool."
  ],
  "quest.2BF5828C4002A4BD.title": "Label the destination",
  "quest.2BF5828C4002A4BD.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Sera kept a written destination beside every connection. Choose one workshop input and label source, destination and spare stock. Hand delivery is a useful fallback during repairs.",
    "Try one small batch and check that its receiver can identify it without asking the sender. Mark this optional observation yourself; the Atlas does not inspect labels or transport."
  ],
  "quest.2D2C52A913E6718A.title": "Leave another harvest possible",
  "quest.2D2C52A913E6718A.quest_desc": [
    "Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Mara counted what remained after a delivery. Harvest one crop batch and one ordinary hive batch, then reserve what each needs to produce again. Separate storage can make reserves easier to see.",
    "Can you repeat both harvests without spending the last planting supply or dismantling the hive? Record your optional answer here; no world detector watches the garden."
  ],
  "quest.7601671FE64DE066.title": "Watch a whole batch",
  "quest.7601671FE64DE066.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful power",
    "",
    "Run a small infuser batch and compare the energy buffer before and after. A machine that flashes on may still lack sustained supply. Keep spare fuel or a second local source for recovery.",
    "If the buffer drains, reduce simultaneous demand and inspect input faces before adding generation. Mark this optional trial after observing it; inventory circuits do not certify a powered workshop."
  ],
  "quest.758AAF75374D9805.title": "Stop before overflow",
  "quest.758AAF75374D9805.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Choose Integrated Dynamics with Integrated Tunnels, or LaserIO. Follow its guide to read a buffer and control insertion. Begin with one item type and a small threshold.",
    "Observe a stop at the threshold, remove a few items, and observe recovery. If transfer continues, check the measured inventory, comparison and output control separately. This optional self-check records your observation; it is not an automatic circuit test."
  ],
  "quest.2011CCEBA6EF8242.title": "Thirty-two arrive together",
  "quest.2011CCEBA6EF8242.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Move 32 ordinary items between containers with configured Modular Routers modules or a Create transfer arrangement. Follow the respective guide for targets and filters; use a batch separate from valuable stock.",
    "Count both ends and check for dropped items. If the destination is full, provide a buffer and retry the same batch. Mark this optional trial once all 32 are accounted for; no detector counts the transfer for you."
  ],
  "quest.17BBD680007901AB.title": "A Shared Language",
  "quest.17BBD680007901AB.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Different benches can now agree on a destination.",
    "Open the Atlas here and explicitly deliver one routing matrix for signal_exchange. That token is consumed; installed machines remain. Gifts are accepted and tutorials are not prerequisites.",
    "If delivery is unavailable, check the listed campaign prerequisites and your inventory. An accepted delivery needs no replay, and this task grants no duplicate item reward."
  ],
  "quest.075794DD2C2DFAA0.title": "Seeds of Continuity",
  "quest.075794DD2C2DFAA0.quest_desc": [
    "Supplies that return",
    "",
    "The garden and hive contribute to the same reserve.",
    "Open the Atlas here and explicitly deliver one propagation core for nursery_protocol. That token is consumed; installed machines remain. Gifts are accepted and tutorials are not prerequisites.",
    "If delivery is unavailable, check the listed campaign prerequisites and your inventory. An accepted delivery needs no replay, and this task grants no duplicate item reward."
  ],
  "quest.55E5576006404510.title": "Power without a Monolith",
  "quest.55E5576006404510.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful power",
    "",
    "Sera left space for several local sources in her drawing.",
    "Open the Atlas here and explicitly deliver one power regulator for distributed_power. That token is consumed; installed machines remain. Gifts are accepted and tutorials are not prerequisites.",
    "If delivery is unavailable, check the listed campaign prerequisites and your inventory. An accepted delivery needs no replay, and this task grants no duplicate item reward."
  ],
  "quest.27A67154B0D96862.title": "When the Shelf is Full",
  "quest.27A67154B0D96862.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "A full shelf can answer before it becomes a blockage.",
    "Open the Atlas here and explicitly deliver one inventory sensor for measured_logistics. That token is consumed; installed machines remain. Gifts are accepted and tutorials are not prerequisites.",
    "If delivery is unavailable, check the listed campaign prerequisites and your inventory. An accepted delivery needs no replay, and this task grants no duplicate item reward."
  ],
  "quest.6C696AA48D00D512.title": "Small Hands, Large Workshops",
  "quest.6C696AA48D00D512.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "A workshop can pass a part onward while keeping its own tools.",
    "Open the Atlas here and explicitly deliver one handling core for workshop_hands. That token is consumed; installed machines remain. Gifts are accepted and tutorials are not prerequisites.",
    "If delivery is unavailable, check the listed campaign prerequisites and your inventory. An accepted delivery needs no replay, and this task grants no duplicate item reward."
  ],
  "quest.6542C13CC523B0E9.title": "Routes of Exchange",
  "quest.6542C13CC523B0E9.quest_desc": [
    "Sera · Local connections",
    "",
    "The Atlas finds a gap between local delivery records, older than the tower's final silence. It may be the first break, or only the first someone wrote down. Five restored routes let you investigate without leaving every workshop waiting on one center.",
    "After all five projects, open the Atlas and deliver three paper and one copper ingot for exchange_route. Those materials are consumed once; there is no item reward. Completed deliveries and installed infrastructure remain as the next act opens."
  ],
  "chapter.5EDFD33D3A393061.title": "IV · Voices of the Atlas",
  "quest.4C15458A9B706E5B.title": "The missing witnesses",
  "quest.4C15458A9B706E5B.quest_desc": [
    "Sera · The lost testimonies",
    "",
    "Sera finds four gaps in the exchanged records. The Atlas remembers a route, but not the people who described it. 'Bring back what they noticed,' she writes, 'and leave room for what we cannot recover.'",
    "Follow four material routes below. Reading and possession tasks teach preparation; only recorded journeys and explicit Atlas deliveries complete campaign milestones. Gifts help with materials but cannot fabricate a visit."
  ],
  "quest.2D6ECC29EBA13A7E.title": "Aether: a witnessed arrival",
  "quest.2D6ECC29EBA13A7E.quest_desc": [
    "Journeys recorded by the team",
    "",
    "Reach Aether. The server records your destination on arrival, or when you log in or respawn there. This can happen in any act: early exploration counts. There is no item to deliver or reward to claim here.",
    "One member's visit counts for the current team campaign. Joining another team does not merge old travels; that team's own record applies. This task mirrors the record and cannot be completed by clicking it."
  ],
  "quest.7FC45742FF7B3AC7.title": "Twilight Forest: a witnessed arrival",
  "quest.7FC45742FF7B3AC7.quest_desc": [
    "Journeys recorded by the team",
    "",
    "Reach Twilight Forest. The server records your destination on arrival, or when you log in or respawn there. This can happen in any act: early exploration counts. There is no item to deliver or reward to claim here.",
    "One member's visit counts for the current team campaign. Joining another team does not merge old travels; that team's own record applies. This task mirrors the record and cannot be completed by clicking it."
  ],
  "quest.5F8D676F685B8FCE.title": "Bumblezone: a witnessed arrival",
  "quest.5F8D676F685B8FCE.quest_desc": [
    "Journeys recorded by the team",
    "",
    "Reach Bumblezone. The server records your destination on arrival, or when you log in or respawn there. This can happen in any act: early exploration counts. There is no item to deliver or reward to claim here.",
    "One member's visit counts for the current team campaign. Joining another team does not merge old travels; that team's own record applies. This task mirrors the record and cannot be completed by clicking it."
  ],
  "quest.04C25D07C0D4FB2A.title": "A crystal tuned to listening",
  "quest.04C25D07C0D4FB2A.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Make Spirit Fire by dropping datura and igniting it with flint and steel, following the Dictionary of Spirits. Transform four diamonds into four spirit-attuned gems in that fire, then craft the gems in a 2×2 square into one spirit-attuned crystal. These are distinct items: the lens needs the crystal, not a single gem. Sera labels its case with a witness’s name."
  ],
  "quest.3BF05DF763333CD9.title": "Two fragments of testimony",
  "quest.3BF05DF763333CD9.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Start Malum without needing soul-stained steel: the crude scythe uses three iron ingots, one refined soulstone and two wooden rods. Smelting raw soulstone yields two refined soulstone. Consult Malum’s guide for spirit collection. Killing a witch with a scythe provides a base two arcane and two wicked spirits; an unrelated weapon does not substitute for the scythe. Reserve two arcane spirits for each spectral lens."
  ],
  "quest.470125DBFA02EAFD.title": "A patient shutter",
  "quest.470125DBFA02EAFD.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Prepare one Create precision mechanism for the spectral lens. Its sequenced assembly has probabilistic output; budget attempts and inspect the native sequence in the recipe viewer. Keep the assembly line from Act III available instead of counting an unfinished intermediate as the finished mechanism."
  ],
  "quest.4066B5E1E0D6EF29.title": "The familiar frame",
  "quest.4066B5E1E0D6EF29.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Craft a calibration frame from two Create iron sheets, two Immersive Engineering copper wires and one raw lens. The spectral recipe consumes this spare frame. The workshop’s earlier delivery did not leave a reusable campaign credit that can replace a physical ingredient."
  ],
  "quest.599BBE74166CEC6E.title": "Assemble the spectral lens",
  "quest.599BBE74166CEC6E.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Combine one spirit-attuned crystal, two arcane spirits, one precision mechanism and one calibration frame in an ordinary crafting grid. This makes one spectral lens. Plan two lenses for this chapter: the archive consumes one, and the containment seal recipe consumes another."
  ],
  "quest.3A81D7FB202BC1EF.title": "A route with a return",
  "quest.3A81D7FB202BC1EF.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "The Aether uses a glowstone portal frame activated with water; return through the portal. For Twilight Forest, prepare a 2×2 water pool with a solid base and a dirt border decorated with flowers, then throw in one diamond. Activation brings lightning: build away from wood and step back. Consult native guidance for progression, pack separate food and mark the return portal. This optional preparation does not record either arrival."
  ],
  "quest.72D8C6025B573FA7.title": "Light above the clouds",
  "quest.72D8C6025B573FA7.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Mine ambrosium ore to collect two ambrosium shards for the horizon chart. Inspect the Aether’s native guidance and the block’s tool requirement before mining. Keep these shards separate from supplies you use during the expedition: the chart needs the physical samples as well as the team’s recorded arrival."
  ],
  "quest.63A78566481EFF47.title": "A forest worked into metal",
  "quest.63A78566481EFF47.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Prepare two ironwood ingots. Twilight Forest’s raw ironwood recipe combines liveroot, raw iron and a gold nugget; smelt the raw ironwood into ingots. Inspect the recipe viewer for batch output before gathering extra materials. Sera keeps the place of collection beside the sample: a material name alone does not tell the story of a journey."
  ],
  "quest.00A91663CFB48B49.title": "Food for the record and the road",
  "quest.00A91663CFB48B49.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Make a spare ration bundle from two vegetable soups and two cooked fish fillets. The horizon chart consumes one bundle and one survey notes item, so bring separate food to eat. Craft replacement survey notes from their recipe if the first survey used your original set."
  ],
  "quest.3DD3BA9CAD0FBB51.title": "Two skies on one page",
  "quest.3DD3BA9CAD0FBB51.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Craft a horizon chart with two ambrosium shards, two ironwood ingots, one survey notes item and one ration bundle. Crafting stays available regardless of act. Before delivery, check that both the Aether and Twilight Forest arrival milestones belong to your current team campaign."
  ],
  "quest.589D6D9B175C666C.title": "Enter as a guest",
  "quest.589D6D9B175C666C.quest_desc": [
    "A living agreement",
    "",
    "The Bumblezone’s native entry uses an ender pearl thrown at a beehive or bee nest. Read its guidance for returning before entering, and mark your starting location. Striking bees or disturbing honey and brood can provoke Wrath; observe before taking anything. Sera’s beekeeper asks visitors to leave a living place behind them. This optional reading never replaces a recorded arrival."
  ],
  "quest.72A9A7677DB57D63.title": "Carry a little of the meadow",
  "quest.72A9A7677DB57D63.quest_desc": [
    "A living agreement",
    "",
    "Gather two pollen puffs in the Bumblezone from pollen piles; consult its native collection guidance and use a tool without Silk Touch. Save this pair for the ecosystem capsule and leave a clear return route. Possessing pollen, including pollen received from a friend, never supplies the separate Bumblezone arrival milestone."
  ],
  "quest.10D4D0C6845BF1A4.title": "Wax from an ordinary hive",
  "quest.10D4D0C6845BF1A4.quest_desc": [
    "A living agreement",
    "",
    "Prepare two Productive Bees wax. Ordinary Minecraft honeycomb can be processed through the native centrifuge route; inspect that recipe and its machine requirements. Specialized breeding is not a prerequisite for this material. Use the Productive Bees guide when choosing later bees, their flowers and breeding ingredients."
  ],
  "quest.155E722412CD338B.title": "Two living supports",
  "quest.155E722412CD338B.quest_desc": [
    "A living agreement",
    "",
    "Prepare two living matrices. Each uses two magebloom fibers, two source gems and one calibration frame; double that list for the capsule. Keep ordinary crops and your working bee setup available. This project asks for crafted materials, not the destruction of a productive garden."
  ],
  "quest.780224C0B0190A32.title": "A small agreement",
  "quest.780224C0B0190A32.quest_desc": [
    "A living agreement",
    "",
    "Combine two pollen puffs, two Productive Bees wax and two living matrices to craft one ecosystem capsule. These are ordinary crafting ingredients; neither breeding a special bee nor an optional observation is a hidden delivery condition. The Atlas separately requires a real Bumblezone arrival."
  ],
  "quest.7201D80B58E95944.title": "A dark edge for the vessel",
  "quest.7201D80B58E95944.quest_desc": [
    "Preserve the unfinished",
    "",
    "Gather two EvilCraft dark gems through the native ore route. Check the ore’s tool requirement and the Origins of Darkness guide before mining unfamiliar deposits. Keep the gems for containment; the project does not ask you to build every EvilCraft machine or offer a living familiar."
  ],
  "quest.13E112503294DBB6.title": "Steel with a remembered purpose",
  "quest.13E112503294DBB6.quest_desc": [
    "Preserve the unfinished",
    "",
    "Use Malum’s Spirit Altar: one iron ingot, four refined soulstone, three wicked spirits, one earthen spirit and one arcane spirit produce one soul-stained steel ingot. Follow the guide for the altar and runewood holders within four blocks. For both ingots, reserve eight refined soulstone, six wicked, two earthen and two arcane spirits. A zombie killed with a scythe has a base one wicked and one earthen spirit. The spare lens needs its own additional spirits."
  ],
  "quest.26ECD64E96DE924C.title": "A second listening glass",
  "quest.26ECD64E96DE924C.quest_desc": [
    "Preserve the unfinished",
    "",
    "Craft a second spectral lens for the containment seal. The first lens delivered to the archive is consumed, so its milestone cannot supply this ingredient. Reuse the same crystal, arcane spirits, precision mechanism and calibration-frame chain; gifts can supply a spare lens without repeating tutorials."
  ],
  "quest.7DB1A841D53C017A.title": "Keep the silence legible",
  "quest.7DB1A841D53C017A.quest_desc": [
    "Preserve the unfinished",
    "",
    "Compare the materials reserved for the archive and the seal before crafting. Sera refuses to fill an unreadable line with a convenient answer: a protected fragment can remain incomplete. Confirm this optional reading after separating the two lenses and checking which one each operation consumes."
  ],
  "quest.429BA86EC20C7A84.title": "Close the vessel gently",
  "quest.429BA86EC20C7A84.quest_desc": [
    "Preserve the unfinished",
    "",
    "Craft one containment seal from two dark gems, two soul-stained steel ingots and one spectral lens. The recipe consumes the spare lens. It does not recover the lens already delivered to the archive, and crafting the seal does not itself complete either narrative project."
  ],
  "quest.4BC3DA06CD2E169A.title": "Voices in the Glass",
  "quest.4BC3DA06CD2E169A.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Sera hears a name before she hears a sentence. Open the Atlas after Routes of Exchange and deliver one spectral lens to the archive. The server consumes that lens once and records the project; keep a second lens for the containment recipe."
  ],
  "quest.6F61C77D6FFCC3F3.title": "Above and Beyond the Canopy",
  "quest.6F61C77D6FFCC3F3.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "The two accounts disagree about the colour of morning. The Atlas keeps both. After Routes of Exchange and recorded arrivals in the Aether and Twilight Forest, open the Atlas and deliver one horizon chart. A gifted chart is accepted, but it cannot replace either journey."
  ],
  "quest.3329AFECCED6CAAD.title": "The Pollinators Agreement",
  "quest.3329AFECCED6CAAD.quest_desc": [
    "A living agreement",
    "",
    "The beekeeper’s account describes a place that continued working after the witnesses left. After Routes of Exchange and a recorded Bumblezone arrival, deliver one ecosystem capsule through the Atlas. The server consumes the capsule; your garden, bees and installed equipment remain useful."
  ],
  "quest.09ED3CB7AB982A11.title": "A Vessel for Restless Memory",
  "quest.09ED3CB7AB982A11.quest_desc": [
    "Preserve the unfinished",
    "",
    "Sera places the unfinished testimony beside the recovered names. After Routes of Exchange and Voices in the Glass, deliver one containment seal through the Atlas. This records preservation, not a claim that every missing word has been recovered; there is no duplicate prototype reward."
  ],
  "quest.360D23E7AD32EF6E.title": "The Atlas keeps their voices",
  "quest.360D23E7AD32EF6E.quest_desc": [
    "Sera · The lost testimonies",
    "",
    "With the archive, horizon survey, pollinators agreement and sealed memory complete, deliver three paper and one copper ingot through the Atlas. This closes Act IV and opens Act V for the team.",
    "Sera writes no single answer over the recovered accounts. The Atlas now carries their differences as carefully as their names. The next workshop will have to build a future that can hold more than one voice."
  ],
  "chapter.068A1E3F716693DD.title": "V · The World We Build",
  "quest.6E93F29B79991680.title": "The line Sera crossed out",
  "quest.6E93F29B79991680.quest_desc": [
    "Sera · The missing plan",
    "",
    "Sera's recovered accounts stop at a drawing of one gate feeding every home. Beside it she sketched three smaller routes, then crossed out the gate. The Atlas kept the answer and lost the reason. Build a network that can pause, a reserve that can renew, and a home whose stores can be read by the next traveler.",
    "This page is an optional reading. The three projects below open after Voices of the Atlas. Only explicit Atlas deliveries record them; possession, crafting and the optional field notes do not."
  ],
  "quest.7B041D8C096D588D.title": "Two alloys for the bypass",
  "quest.7B041D8C096D588D.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Reserve two Mekanism atomic alloys for the Ark bus. In the Metallurgic Infuser, one reinforced alloy takes one infused alloy and 20 diamond infusion; one atomic alloy then takes one reinforced alloy and 40 refined-obsidian infusion. Check JEI for the earlier inputs. Ivo marks the finished pair as replaceable stock so a failed request need not strip the working machines."
  ],
  "quest.3B42EB9382C43AAF.title": "A second path for the order",
  "quest.3B42EB9382C43AAF.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Prepare two PneumaticCraft printed circuit boards. The initial native route makes an Empty PCB in a Pressure Chamber, exposes it in a UV Light Box, then etches it into an unassembled PCB; insufficient exposure can fail the etch. The printed board uses one unassembled PCB, two capacitors and two transistors. Consult JEI for each stage and keep the earlier workshop equipment in service. This possession lesson does not consume the boards."
  ],
  "quest.616121CD1220D7F0.title": "Keep the hands at work",
  "quest.616121CD1220D7F0.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Set aside two handling cores for the bus recipe. Each draws on the Act III route of blank router modules, a Create precision mechanism and a power regulator; plan two complete sets in JEI. Put a small input and output buffer around the workshop line so a stopped transfer leaves its materials visible. Keep the installed routers doing useful work while the new cores become ingredients."
  ],
  "quest.6C6D77098E537A3C.title": "Know what the buffer holds",
  "quest.6C6D77098E537A3C.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Add one inventory sensor to the bus recipe. Revisit the Act III route through Menril chunks, LaserIO logic chips and a routing matrix. Before changing throughput, choose a lower stock level that should pause a job and an upper level that should stop refilling. Put those numbers beside a real buffer; the important reading is what remains after a batch, not how fast items pass through it."
  ],
  "quest.765DEE642FC97F72.title": "A bus with a way around",
  "quest.765DEE642FC97F72.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "In an ordinary crafting grid combine two atomic alloys, two printed circuit boards, two handling cores and one inventory sensor: seven slots make one Ark bus. Trace a material from input buffer to output, then mark where you would pause, refill and resume it if one route failed. The prototype is for the Atlas; keep useful transport installed for the next order."
  ],
  "quest.612B6CF528DB5881.title": "Field note: empty, refill, resume",
  "quest.612B6CF528DB5881.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported exercise: label one input buffer, record its starting count, stop its supply and let a small job draw it down. Restore the supply and check that the next batch finishes once, with the expected remainder. Stop safely if a recipe lacks input; a paused job is recoverable. The checkmark records your observation, not automatic machine validation or campaign progress."
  ],
  "quest.7A6A246A99FABD76.title": "A Network that Recovers",
  "quest.7A6A246A99FABD76.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "After Voices of the Atlas, deliver one Ark bus through the Atlas to record the team's resilient backbone. The Atlas consumes that prototype once; the buffer exercise remains your optional rehearsal. Ivo leaves a space on the plan for a failed line to be repaired without taking the rest of the settlement apart."
  ],
  "quest.6A0476FB91872873.title": "Metal from an open sky",
  "quest.6A0476FB91872873.quest_desc": [
    "A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Reserve two Nature's Aura sky ingots. At a flower-decorated Offering Table, one infused iron yields one sky ingot, or one tainted gold yields two. The native book teaches the offering bowl and a Spirit of Calling dropped nearby. Its recipe makes three spirits from Overworld and Nether aura bottles, a diamond, infused iron and tainted gold; plan Nether access. Choose the one-ingot or two-ingot route in JEI before committing your aura stock."
  ],
  "quest.1CCC9F83FE8B9B51.title": "A harvest with a ceiling",
  "quest.1CCC9F83FE8B9B51.quest_desc": [
    "A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Prepare two Mystical Agriculture imperium essences. The native essence ladder combines four tertium and an infusion crystal for one imperium; each lower step also takes four, so two imperium budget eight tertium or 128 inferium. The crystal is reusable, but check its remaining durability. The Infusion Altar is for seed recipes, not this essence ladder. Start inferium through native mining, mob drops or growing, then choose a bounded batch your existing plot can replace."
  ],
  "quest.60C09916BD96526A.title": "Carry the habitat forward",
  "quest.60C09916BD96526A.quest_desc": [
    "A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Set aside two ecosystem capsules. Each uses two Bumblezone pollen puffs, two Productive Bees wax and two living matrices; check your Act IV route before budgeting a pair. Keep the hive and wax processing in service, and leave a little stock for the next capsule. Mara draws this reserve beside the crop plot because neither one should have to drain the other."
  ],
  "quest.409935D6C0EBDC29.title": "Leave the nursery growing",
  "quest.409935D6C0EBDC29.quest_desc": [
    "A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Add two propagation cores from the Act III recipe or from exchange. A core combines prudentium essence, bee wax and a living matrix, so budget its stock separately from the new imperium and capsules. Measure one small nursery replenishment cycle before increasing throughput. Keeping the nursery installed makes the second batch a repeatable job rather than a one-time sacrifice."
  ],
  "quest.6F3334D0429BBA36.title": "The reserve's engine",
  "quest.6F3334D0429BBA36.quest_desc": [
    "A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Combine two sky ingots, two imperium essences, two ecosystem capsules and two propagation cores in an ordinary crafting grid. Eight slots make one renewal engine. Before assembling it, look at the remaining garden, hive and aura supplies. If one route cannot repeat a small batch, reduce demand there instead of adding another field just to fill a single recipe."
  ],
  "quest.5DE0AEDC6388B1EE.title": "Field note: take one, grow one",
  "quest.5DE0AEDC6388B1EE.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported exercise: take one bounded batch from the crop route, one from the hive route and one from the aura route you already use. Record what each consumes or waits for, then let those inputs recover before repeating. Change a local limit if a buffer keeps overflowing. The checkmark records your judgment; it does not measure regeneration or require loaded chunks while you are away."
  ],
  "quest.0FA172F312611EF8.title": "Renewable Horizons",
  "quest.0FA172F312611EF8.quest_desc": [
    "A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "After Voices of the Atlas, deliver one renewal engine through the Atlas. It consumes that prototype once and records the team's renewal project. Mara writes beside the reserve: 'Take only what can grow back before the next traveler needs it.' Use the optional harvest note to test whether your own limits answer her."
  ],
  "quest.2BA2EF5E6E24A403.title": "Two meals before departure",
  "quest.2BA2EF5E6E24A403.quest_desc": [
    "A place to return to",
    "",
    "Prepare two Farmer's Delight fish stews for the habitation contract. The native Cooking Pot recipe accepts fish through its raw-fish ingredient tag, with tomato sauce and onion; check JEI for the pack's current matching fish and serving step. Mara keeps a separate serving for travelers: the two stews committed to the prototype are not the settlement's entire food reserve."
  ],
  "quest.3B412771A4C57233.title": "Something fresh on the shelf",
  "quest.3B412771A4C57233.quest_desc": [
    "A place to return to",
    "",
    "Prepare two Farmer's Delight mixed salads. Its native shapeless recipe combines a leafy green, tomato, beetroot and bowl; check JEI for the accepted greens. Leave the kitchen able to make another meal after these are committed. Sera's oldest room has a table and a spare bowl; it was a place for another person, not a trophy case for one perfect dish."
  ],
  "quest.77320E2B7BDC2510.title": "A count the next person can read",
  "quest.77320E2B7BDC2510.quest_desc": [
    "A place to return to",
    "",
    "Add one AE2 calculation processor to the habitation contract. Check the native inscriber route in JEI and keep the workshop that made it available. The processor belongs to the prototype; a written stock count, a chest label or another clear local record can make the real pantry understandable without requiring a larger network."
  ],
  "quest.7CDE8A7F14D2DA00.title": "Food for the road and the return",
  "quest.7CDE8A7F14D2DA00.quest_desc": [
    "A place to return to",
    "",
    "Reserve two ration bundles from the earlier pantry recipe: each combines two vegetable soups and two cooked fish fillets. Budget those separately from the new fish stew and salad; they feed different parts of the habitation contract. Keep ordinary meals reachable for eating while the kitchen prepares the next order. A full contract with empty shelves would be a poor welcome."
  ],
  "quest.7D7BB71A417C6A1F.title": "A contract for an inhabited place",
  "quest.7D7BB71A417C6A1F.quest_desc": [
    "A place to return to",
    "",
    "Combine two fish stews, two mixed salads, one calculation processor and two ration bundles in an ordinary crafting grid. Seven slots make one habitation contract; the four bowls from the stews and salads return through normal crafting remainders. Put those bowls back into the kitchen. Furniture and installed equipment remain in the room, ready to serve another group."
  ],
  "quest.64A39E89998AE121.title": "Field note: a room someone can use",
  "quest.64A39E89998AE121.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported exercise: walk from the arrival point to a lit sleeping place, a reachable kitchen and a pantry with legible stock. Ask whether someone else could find food and replenish one mixed order without you explaining the layout. Choose one shared hall or several small homes. A checkmark records your walk-through; the game does not inspect comfort, signs or architecture."
  ],
  "quest.41D22D9557C9E920.title": "A Place Worth Returning To",
  "quest.41D22D9557C9E920.quest_desc": [
    "A place to return to",
    "",
    "After Voices of the Atlas, deliver one habitation contract through the Atlas. It consumes the contract once and records settlement supply for the team. The optional room tour is your own design test. Mara sets a spare bowl on Sera's old table; the next visitor should find food, light and a place to sleep without having to ask where everything went."
  ],
  "quest.49D5419C7B57F699.title": "Field note: a visible pause",
  "quest.49D5419C7B57F699.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported exercise: if you enjoy ComputerCraft, build a small panel that displays a buffer count and a paused or running label. If you prefer no code, a sign and a manual stop work for the same observation. Compare the displayed count with the actual container before and after one batch. This note cannot gate the Ark bus delivery."
  ],
  "quest.2186E0A1EC9CA518.title": "The World We Build",
  "quest.2186E0A1EC9CA518.quest_desc": [
    "Sera · The missing plan",
    "",
    "Sera's last recovered line reads: 'The gate was efficient until it failed. The homes survived because each kept something the others could share.' When the three projects are recorded, deliver three paper and one copper ingot through the Atlas to close the world network. The server consumes those four materials once and gives no item reward.",
    "The Atlas now opens the way to Act VI manually. A working settlement remains behind you; leaving is a choice, and returning should still mean something."
  ]
}
